CHMOD - change file permissions
Usage: chmod <mode> <path>
       chown <user[:group]> <path>

Records Unix-style permissions for a path (for example 644 or
755). Protected paths like /etc refuse writes from non-root users.

Examples:
  chmod 600 secret.txt
  sudo chown root /etc/motd.txt

Notes:
- ls -l shows the recorded mode and owner.
- chown requires root.
